// PARAM: --analysis interval --globals join --program-globals flow-insensitive
// Seidl, Vojdani, Erhard, Schwarz, "Mixed Flow-Sensitive Static Analysis:
// Engineering Modularity" (FM 2026), Example 1: is a flow-insensitive summary
// of g enough to rule out the error g > 42? The program is Fig. 1 without h
// (01-fig1_sequential_globals.vimp), so g is the only global.
//
// With program globals on the shared channel, g is one fact every point
// reads. Its contributions 0 (the default), 1, -17 and 42 join to [-17,42]:
// the summary still proves g < 43, but not g == 42. With --program-globals
// local g travels flow-sensitively and both checks are proved.
global g;
fun f() {
  g = 42;
}
fun main() {
  g = 1;
  g = -17;
  f();
  __voblint_check(g == 42); // UNKNOWN
  __voblint_check(g < 43); // PROVED
}
